Segment Insights & Regional Overview
By Type — Oral vs. Parenteral Therapies
Parenteral formulations—especially intrathecal biologics—currently dominate the market due to high clinical efficacy. However, oral therapies are expanding rapidly, supported by their convenience, home-based administration potential, and strong pipeline representation.
By Application
Approved Therapies hold the largest share, driven by strong adoption and guideline inclusion.
Late Stage Candidates represent the fastest-growing segment, fueled by next-generation gene therapies and splicing modulators entering pivotal trials.
By End User
Hospitals remain the central hub for SMA diagnosis and high-complexity neuro-therapeutic procedures, while specialty neuromuscular clinics show steady expansion due to focused long-term care needs.
By Therapeutic Approach
•	SMN2 Splicing Modulation leads the current treatment paradigm.
•	SMN1 Gene Replacement remains a breakthrough category with potential near-curative outcomes.
•	Neuroprotection is rising as a complementary treatment strategy.
